================================================================================
Reference implementations
================================================================================

No code from the following was copied into mlx-serve. They were read as
specifications while writing our own implementations of the same kernels, and
they are listed because they made that work possible.

  * Layr-Labs/mlxfast-bonsai2-27b-engine (MIT), the reference for the few-row
    2-bit tensor path in `src/qmv_nax2.zig`: its `qmm_m16_block` fragment
    coordinate mapping, the 256-k weight line loaded across a fragment quad and
    exchanged with `simd_shuffle`, the dequantize-into-the-right-operand
    arrangement, and the two-slice threadgroup reduction. Transcribed into a
    JIT `metal_kernel` here, not shipped as their source.
  * Layr-Labs/mlxfast-bonsai2-27b-engine (MIT), the reference for the 2-bit
    simdgroup-MMA verify kernel in `src/qmv2.zig` (`msv_qmv2_mma`): its
    `FewRowPackedMatmul` fragment coordinate mapping, two codes per lane
    decoded straight into the weight fragment, and per-group scaling of the
    partial products. Transcribed into a JIT `metal_kernel` here, not shipped
    as their source.
  * Layr-Labs/mlxfast-bonsai2-27b-engine (MIT), the reference for the opt-in
    int8 prefill in `src/qmm_int8.zig`: its register-staged prompt matmul (2-bit
    codes expanded to int8 straight into the tensor op's operand, signed
    per-group activation codes quantized with the rotation) and the factored
    ternary epilogue. Written as a JIT `metal_kernel` here, not shipped as their
    source.

